{
  "schema": "catalog-conformance-supplement/1",
  "note": "2026-11-15 #2434 every doorway a real door. Forty new immutable revisions, one per core building def (core-<name>@3; core-hall@4), each built on its door-fitted revision (wall-doorways-20261114): make.args.doorThings 2 leaves every doorway bare (inside, upstairs, onto a balcony) for a core/door@2 placed in it (templates, and door-fit/2 at boot in live worlds); an inside doorway is widened toward 1.2 m after every other opening has its place, where its wall has room. Older revisions keep their bytes. A K=2 run of `conformance.mjs --k 2 --filter <ref>` for each new revision placed, baked, furnished and rendered every sample of all 40 defs (61 samples each). The findings (gallery-budget/triangles: 73, place/architecture: 3 pins) are gallery triangle budgets at large sizes and many floors, and layout findings from the generator's plans: core-lighthouse@3 (no entrance, at wallThickness.max and one random sample) and core-roundhouse@3 (no entrance at one random sample), the kinds already pinned for core-lighthouse@1/@2 and core-roundhouse@1 (known-20261015, wall-doorways-20261114). The architecture checks of every revision equal its door-fitted revision's over a 1920-layout sweep (floors 1-3, widths and depths 4-12 m). They are pinned here by the new hashes. No budgets, samples or gap checks were relaxed.",
